Now that you’ve mastered catching bad transactions and fake IDs, we’re moving on to the big boss of financial decisions\: Credit Scoring. Up until now, you were just stopping bad actors at the door. Starting today, you’re deciding who actually gets the money and how much they get.
So here’s the corporate line on Credit Scoring\: 'Empower responsible borrowers while safeguarding company liquidity.' Basically, upper management wants to maximize interest returns from solid applicants, but Mr. Angilo still wants us to give borderline applicants a chance to build up their score instead of instantly shutting the door on them.
Some tips on CredScoring, Don’t just look at their current income or debt. Look at their payment history, their loan ratio, and what they’re actually using the money for. A high-risk score doesn't always mean a bad borrower, but a low income with zero repayment plan will sink your metrics fast.
Your terminal has now access to CreditScoring, and again… your digital assistant will assist you there. Good to the luck, my dudes.